diff --git a/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-autoescape/design.md b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-autoescape/design.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8a45f96
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-autoescape/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+## Context
+
+`App.select_jinja_autoescape` currently determines the default by comparing
+the filename suffix against a fixed tuple of lowercase supported extensions.
+
+## Decision
+
+Normalize the filename only for the suffix comparison, then retain the
+existing supported-extension tuple and `None` branch. This is focused,
+preserves extension matching semantics, and avoids altering custom autoescape
+configuration.
+
+## Verification
+
+Exercise supported mixed-case extensions as well as the existing unsupported
+and `None` behavior, then run the public test command.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-autoescape/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-autoescape/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cb05e8d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-autoescape/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Case-insensitive default autoescape extensions
+
+## Why
+
+Flask's default Jinja autoescape selector recognizes supported template
+extensions only when they are lowercase. Templates such as `invoice.HTML`
+therefore render with autoescaping disabled even though `invoice.html` does
+not.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Treat the default supported Jinja template extensions case-insensitively.
+- Preserve the existing behavior for unsupported extensions and an absent
+  filename.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `App.select_jinja_autoescape` and its tests.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-autoescape/specs/template-autoescape/spec.md b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-autoescape/specs/template-autoescape/spec.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3864d10
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-autoescape/specs/template-autoescape/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Default template-extension autoescaping is case-insensitive
+
+The default Jinja autoescape selector SHALL enable autoescaping for the
+supported `.html`, `.htm`, `.xml`, `.xhtml`, and `.svg` extensions regardless
+of the filename's letter case.
+
+#### Scenario: Mixed-case supported extension
+
+- **WHEN** the selector receives a filename ending in a supported extension
+  with uppercase or mixed-case letters
+- **THEN** it returns `True`
+
+#### Scenario: Unsupported or absent filename
+
+- **WHEN** the selector receives a filename without a supported extension
+- **THEN** it returns `False`
+- **WHEN** the selector receives `None`
+- **THEN** it returns `True`
